      "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=10,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}X].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}X] & ={(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{4}\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
